    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1182">

                <pb facs="1089" n="831" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg831"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111Ei9/26</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The</hi>
                    
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>
                    
                    <hi rendition="#italic">to the Assistant Secretary of the Treasury</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Peters</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-04-02">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 2, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your letter April 2<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1182-f1"/> enclosing Commander
                    Thierichens’s letter of March 29. Department recommends that collector of
                    customs inform Commander Thierichens of departure of belligerent merchant
                    vessels of Germany’s adversaries, as requested by him.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1182-f1" n="1" xml:id="d1182-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed. See letter of March 29, <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref
                        target="#pg829">p. 829</ref>.</p>
